original_source_statement_tex:
\label{lemma-relative-inertia-as-fibre-product}
Let $F : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{S}'$ be a $1$-morphism of categories
fibred over a category $\mathcal{C}$. Then the diagram
$$
\xymatrix{
\mathcal{I}_{\mathcal{S}/\mathcal{S}'}
\ar[d]_{F \circ (\ref{equation-inertia-structure-map})}
\ar[rr]_{(\ref{equation-comparison})} & &
\mathcal{I}_\mathcal{S} \ar[d]^{(\ref{equation-functorial})} \\
\mathcal{S}' \ar[rr]^e & &
\mathcal{I}_{\mathcal{S}'}
}
$$
is a $2$-fibre product.

statement:
Let $\mathcal C$ be a category and $F:\mathcal S\to\mathcal S'$ a $1$-morphism of categories fibred over $\mathcal C$. Write $\mathcal I_{\mathcal S}$ and $\mathcal I_{\mathcal S'}$ for the inertia categories of pairs $(x,\alpha)$ with $\alpha$ an automorphism, and write $\mathcal I_{\mathcal S/\mathcal S'}$ for pairs $(x,\alpha)$ in $\mathcal S$ with $F(\alpha)=\mathrm{id}_{F(x)}$ (morphisms in each inertia category commute with their automorphisms). Let $\pi:\mathcal I_{\mathcal S/\mathcal S'}\to\mathcal S$ send $(x,\alpha)\mapsto x$, let $c:\mathcal I_{\mathcal S/\mathcal S'}\to\mathcal I_{\mathcal S}$ be the comparison, let $\mathcal I_F:\mathcal I_{\mathcal S}\to\mathcal I_{\mathcal S'}$ send $(x,\alpha)\mapsto(F(x),F(\alpha))$, and let $e:\mathcal S'\to\mathcal I_{\mathcal S'}$ be the neutral section $y\mapsto(y,\mathrm{id}_y)$. Then the square
$$
\xymatrix{
\mathcal I_{\mathcal S/\mathcal S'}\ar[r]^c\ar[d]_{F\circ\pi}
&\mathcal I_{\mathcal S}\ar[d]^{\mathcal I_F}\\
\mathcal S'\ar[r]^e &\mathcal I_{\mathcal S'}
}
$$
is a $2$-fibre product square.

